{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Let them rejoice</b> — by giving their dew, and the earth gives its produce, and the field gives its fruit, and this is <b>יעלוז</b>." "And the meaning of <b>ירעם</b> — the clouds rising from the sea, or the whole is by way of parable, for the entire world will be in tranquility and security when the righteousness of HaShem is seen in the earth, or after the manner of the princes and musicians going forth before the king when he comes from a distant place." "And the meaning of <b>כי בא</b> — the second sense follows the first, like: <b>אל החצר החיצונה אל העם</b>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 96, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:27.351065393Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}